1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Also known as Tode Mangu the Moslem (ref: 1280 http://s155239215.onlinehome.us/turkic/70_Dateline/kipchak_dateline_Ru.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Tuda Mangu was a very devout muslim, observing strict fasts and always surrounded with sheikhs and fakirs, but he was an incapable ruler. He had to abdicate and was replaced on the throne by Tula Buqa, nephew of the two preceding 
2 CONC khans. (p.401 of  The Empire of the Steppes: A History of Central Asia By René Grousset)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==
2 CONT Mengu-Timur was succeeded in 1281 by his brother Töde Möngke, who was a Muslim. He made his peace with Kublai, returned his sons to him, and acknowledged his supremacy.[38][39] Nogai and Köchü, Khan of the White Horde and son of O
2 CONC rda Khan, also made peace with the Yuan Dynasty and the Ilkhanate. According to Mamluk historians, Töde Möngke sent the Mamluks a letter proposing to fight against their common enemy the unbelieving Ilkhanate. This indicates that 
2 CONC he might have had an interest in Azerbaijan and Georgia both of which were ruled by the Ilkhans. https://www.podgorski.com/main/khanate-golden-horde.html
2 CONT ==
