1 OCCU Khan of Western Chagatai Khanate
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Soyurghatmïsh Khan (died 1384) was Khan of the Western Chagatai Khanate (1370–1384). He was the son of Danishmendji, of the House of Ogedei.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Timur gained control of the territory of the western Chagatai Khanate in the 1360s, he did not abolish the office of khan. Instead, in order to legitimatize his authority, he placed on the throne Suurgatmish, that was not a m
2 CONC ember of the house of Chagatai Khan, but from the house of Ogedei. Timur ruled as an amir in Suurgatmish's name. The khan, however, was only a ceremonial figure, and Timur held all of the power within the state. Upon Suurgatmish's
2 CONC  death in 1384, he was replaced by his son Sultan Mahmud.
2 CONT
2 CONT His daughter named Urun Sultan Khanika was married to Timur's son Miran Shah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by: Khabul Shah	Western Chagatai Khan 1370–1384	Followed by: Sultan Mahmud
