2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Sheikh-Uwais-I-Sadegh-Moez-Al-din-Oveys-Jalayer-r-1356-1374-%D8%B4%DB%8C%D8%AE-%D8%A7%D9%88%DB%8C%D8%B3-%D8%A8%D9%87%D8%A7%D8%AF%D8%B1%D8%AE%D8%A7%D9%86/6000000038867727298
2 CONT
2 CONT attacked Tabriz and in 1380 AD entered it. In this way Azarbaijan too fell in the hands of the Jalayerians. ] ref p.194 of  The Book of Iran. Iranian History at a Glance2005 by Reza Shabani and Mahmood Farrokhpey.
2 CONT
2 CONT ["Berdi Beg (or Berdibek) was Khan of the Golden Horde from 1357 till 1359, succeeding his father Jani Beg of whom Berdi Beg may have been behind the poisoning. [ Howorth records that Jani Beg returned to Kipchak and, falling ill,
2 CONC  summoned his son Berdi Beg to install him as his successor but that “fearing that his father might recover, Berdibeg murdered him”, adding that “according to Russian authors, he proceeded to put to death twelve of his brothers” o
2 CONC n his accession]
2 CONT
2 CONT His reign was marked by turmoil and political murders, and in 1359 he was assassinated by his brother Qulpa, after which the Golden Horde fell apart. He had one unnamed daughter [ Tulunbeg] who was the wife of Mamai."] ref: https:
2 CONC //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berdi_Beg
