1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On 26 Šaʿbān 861/19 July 1457, the Timurid ruler Sultan Abu Saʿid conquered Herat. He treated Gowhar-šād well, but when he was informed that she was sharing information with Ebrāhim b. ʿAlāʾ-al-Dowla, and that the 
2 CONC powerful Šir Ḥāji, fearing for his own life as the murderer of Tarḵān amirs, would not serve him while Gowhar-šād was alive, he had her executed on 9 Ramażān 861/31 July 1457 (Maṭlaʿ-e saʿdayn, ed. Šafiʿ, II/2, pp. 1143-44; Ḥabib 
2 CONC al-siar, Tehran, IV, pp. 67-69).
