2 CONT
2 CONT Chief Rabbi and Court Jew to Alfons V (the African King of Portugal).  Shlomo fathered at least three sons: 1) Gedaliah, 2) David, 3) Yaakob; It is possible that Yaakob is the adopted son of Gedaliah.  He was rabbi of the Lisbon c
2 CONC ommunity, and forbade his children and relatives to accumulate property because he foresaw the coming persecutions.  His death occurred before that of Alfonso V.  '''Shlomo 	was a math teacher of Afonso de Albuquerque''' – Afonso 
2 CONC was anointed viceroy and "Duke of Goa" by 	King Manuel I of Portugal, being the first Portuguese duke not from the royal family, and the first 	Portuguese title landed overseas. .
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Citado no livro de Elías Lipiner: O tempo dos Judeus: segundo as Ordenações do Reino, página 127, seria o tio de Judá Negro, e membro da família "Ibn Yahia" de Lisboa, e ainda conforme o mesmo livro, seria irmão de Guedelha Negro,
2 CONC  Logo foi possível identifica-lo como "Shlomo ben David ben Shlomo ibn Yachya" nascido em 1430, e falecido em 1490, na cidade de Lisboa, e então foi possível mesclar o perfil, e fazer a devida dedução.
2 CONT
