1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khanzada_Begum
2 CONT
2 CONT Khanzada Begum Timurid princess Padshah Begum
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse	Shaybani Khan - Sayyid Hada - Mahdi Khwaja - Issue	: Khurram Shah
2 CONT
2 CONT Khanzada Begum (c. 1478 – 1545) was a Timurid princess and the eldest daughter of Umar Shaikh Mirza II, the amir of Ferghana. She was also the dearly beloved older sister of Babur, the founder of the Mughal Empire. She and her bro
2 CONC ther remained deeply attached to each other all their lives, a period during which the family progressed from ruling a tiny and obscure principality in Central Asia to ruling a large portion of the Indian subcontinent. Babur confe
2 CONC rred on his sister, the honorable title of Padshah Begum and she was really the first lady of his Empire after his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Khanzada Begum is frequently mentioned in the Baburnama, her brother's memoirs, and always with affection and respect. She is also frequently mentioned in the Humayun-nama by her niece Gulbadan Begum, who calls her aunt 'Dearest L
2 CONC ady' (aka janam). Many occasions are described where she intervened during political difficulties between her relatives and more specifically her nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT [Shaybiini Khan proposed to mako peace with  Babur, if ho would give his sister Khan-Zada Bogum in marriago to him. "Babur  Padishah gave up Khan-Zada Begum in exchange for his own life and escaped." ]
2 CONT
2 CONT [... Khan-Zada *Begum was sent  with honour to her brother Babur n . This lady had fallen into the hands of  Shaybani Khan at Samarqand in the summer of 906 12 /1501, and had borne  him a son, Khurram Shah Sultan, who was appointe
2 CONC d governor of Balkh  in 913 13 /1507. Subsequently, she was divorced out of fear that she might,  in concert with her brother, plot against her husband's life. She was then  given in marriage to Sayyicl Hadi, who fell fighting for
2 CONC  Shaybani Khan in  the battle against Shah Isma'il u . ] page 63 of https://archive.org/stream/HistoryOfShahIsmailSafawi-GhulamSarwar/119900259-History-of-Shah-Isma-il-Safawi-Ghulam-Sarwar_djvu.txt
