2 CONT
2 CONT Fyodor II Borisovich Godunov of Russia (Russian: Фёдор II Борисович) (1589 - 10 June/20 June 1605) was a tsar of Russia (1605) during the Time of Troubles. He was born in Moscow, the son and successor to Boris Godunov. His mother 
2 CONC Maria Grigorievna Skuratova-Belskaya was one of the daughters of Malyuta Skuratov, the infamous favourite of Ivan the Terrible.
2 CONT --------------------
