1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eldest son in a family, for longevity was names "Nestor" or "Never-Old"
2 CONT
2 CONT Pavel Ivanovich Sapiega (c. 1490 - 1579) was a Lithuanian statesman and military figure. The statesman of Braslav (1517–1547), the economic marshal (1519–1557), the voivode of Podlasie (1556–1558) and the voivode of Novgorod from 
2 CONC 1558.
2 CONT
2 CONT He came from the Koden family lineage of the magnate family Sapiega / Sapieha with the coat of arms "Fox", the son of Ivan and his first wife. He had brothers Mikhail and Fedor. He studied at the University of Krakow.
2 CONT
2 CONT He took part in the war with the Muscovite state in 1534-1535, and in the Influential War (1558-1582) in 1561.
2 CONT
2 CONT He took part in eight Diets during 1559-1568. He was an opponent of the Lublin Union, but signed the union act. He professed Orthodoxy, at a certain time of his life - Calvinism.
2 CONT
2 CONT For the first time he married Helena of Halshany / Alshenai, with whom he had sons Alexander, Nikolai and Bogdan, as well as daughters Bogdan and Marina. For the second time he married Alexandra Hodkevich, with whom he had a son A
2 CONC ndrey, as well as daughters Vasilisa, Raina and Maryna. Pavel Sapiega / Sapieha was buried in the church of St. Trinity in Vilnius.
