1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The founder of the Orthodox church in the village of Hołuble in Podlasie (recorded in 1545) was Bohdana, the wife of Jan Steczko. Her daughter, Anna Romanovna Drucka Lubiecka, was adopted by Jan Steczko because he 
2 CONC had no children of his own.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1508, the village of Rogów (Podlasie) was purchased from the last member of the Sepieński family — Stanisław Sokołowski (the grandson of Mikołaj Sepieński) — by Jan Steckowicz (Steczko) Dołubowski, coat of arms Łabędź (Swan), c
2 CONC alled Cybulka (died before 1541). He served as starosta of Drohiczyn (1501–1508) and court marshal of the Grand Duchy (1520–1541).
2 CONT
2 CONT His adopted daughter Anna, who married Mikołaj Ostyk, the starosta of Krewo, founded an Orthodox church dedicated to St. Demetrius in 1546.
2 CONT A record of this foundation was entered in the Drohiczyn books in 1644.
2 CONT
