1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mehmed I Giray (Mukhamad Khan Girai) known as Great (b.1465 – d.1523) — was a khan of the Crimean Khanate in 1515 –1523.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Meñli I Giray, inherited power after his father's death. In 1520 signed a temporary alliance with the king of Poland and the Grand Duke of Lithuania, Zygmunt I "The Old", against Muscovy. In 1521 he took Kazan, where he put
2 CONC  his brother, Sahib I Giray (future Khan of Crimea, too) in power. Leading a large Tatar army he defeated Vasili III of Russia near Moscow.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mehmed_I_Giray
