1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Yunus Khan (c. 1416–1487) (Uyghur: يونس خان‎), was Khan of Moghulistan from 1462 until his death. He is identified by many historians with Ḥājjī `Ali (Chinese: 哈只阿力, Pinyin: Hazhi Ali) (Uyghur: ھاجى علي‎), of the c
2 CONC ontemporary Chinese records.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yunus Ali was the eldest son of Uwais Khan of Moghulistan. When Vais Khan was killed in 1428 AD, the Moghuls were split as to who should succeed him. Although Yunus Khan was his eldest son, the majority favored Yunus' younger brot
2 CONC her, Esen Buqa.[1] As a result, he and his supporters fled to Ulugh Beg, the Timurid ruler of Transoxiana, who however imprisoned the group. He gave Yunus Khan to his father, Shah Rukh, who treated him well, and who sent him to le
2 CONC arn under Maulana Sharaf ad-Din Ali Yazdi. Yunus Khan spent several years learning under the Maulana in Yazd, in the process becoming one of the most educated Moghuls. After the Maulana died he wandered for some time before settli
2 CONC ng on Shiraz as a home.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Yunus Ali was the eldest son of Uwais Khan of Moghulistan. When Vais Khan was killed in 1428 AD, the Moghuls were split as to who should succeed him. Although Yunus Khan was his eldest son, the majority favored Yunus' younger brot
2 CONC her, Esen Buqa.[1] As a result, he and his supporters fled to Ulugh Beg, the Timurid ruler of Transoxiana, who however imprisoned the group. He gave Yunus Khan to his father, Shah Rukh, who treated him well, and who sent him to le
2 CONC arn under Maulana Sharaf ad-Din Ali Yazdi. Yunus Khan spent several years learning under the Maulana in Yazd, in the process becoming one of the most educated Moghuls. After the Maulana died he wandered for some time before settli
2 CONC ng on Shiraz as a home.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Khan of Moghulestan'''
