1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gouverneur de Maragheh Gouverneur de Rezayieh et de Tabriz sous Mozaffareddin Shah (1896-1907) et Mohamad Ali Shah (1907-1909)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Le fils de Ahmad Khan Moghadam, prit 3 armees de fantassins, 260 cavaliers et 120 fusiliers de l'armee de l'Azarbaijan et les conduisit de Maragheh a Harat, a la suite deu Sultan Murad Mirza Hassan ol Saltaneh et fut le premier a 
2 CONC entrer dans Herat. Son petit fils Eskandar, le fils de Hossein Pasha,  y fut tue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ref: زندگی و زمانه احمد کسروی: در برگیرنده: زندگانی من، ده سال در عدلیه، چرا از ... By Mohammad Amini, محمد امینی‎ taper: حسین پاشاخان مقدم مراغه فرزند کی بود؟
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [Hossein Pasha Khan II had one son Iskender khan]
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Iskandar Khan Moghadam was the son and direct generational successor of Haj Hossein Khan Moghadam Javanshir. [1]
2 CONT When tracking this specific line on the ground in Maragheh, Iskandar Khan followed his father’s footsteps directly into the Qajar military apparatus: [1, 2]
2 CONT •	The Military Career: Like his father (the general and ambassador) and his grandfather (Ahmed Khan), Iskandar Khan was a highly trained battlefield officer. He served as a senior commander in the military forces of Azerbaijan, sp
2 CONC ecifically leading regiments of the elite Moghadam cavalry. [1, 2]
2 CONT •	His Death in Battle: Iskandar Khan's career was cut short when he was killed in action during an imperial campaign against the Turkmen tribes in the Gorgan (Goklan) desert near Astrabad. Following his death, he was buried locall
2 CONC y in Astrabad. [1]
2 CONT •	The Continuation of the Title: Tracing the line further down, Iskandar Khan was the father of Fatehollah Khan Shuja-ed-Dowleh, who in turn fathered the notorious late-19th and early-20th century ruler of Maragheh, Samad Khan Shu
2 CONC ja al-Dawla. [1]
2 CONT By identifying Iskandar Khan as the link, the succession line for the ruling military branch in Maragheh stays tightly aligned: Ahmed Khan \(\rightarrow \) Haj Hossein Khan \(\rightarrow \) Iskandar Khan \(\rightarrow \) Fateholla
2 CONC h Khan \(\rightarrow \) Samad Khan. [1, 2]
