1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Archival sources preserve court records concerning the murder of Elena Monwid Dorohostayska (after marriage Charlinska / sometimes Charlecka) of her husband Szczęsny (Shchensny) Charlinski of Charleża. The crime to
2 CONC ok place in August 1604 at his estate Lubcza.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the investigation records, Elena planned the murder together with servants. The crime involved the servant Andrzej Rozhkowski (who later confessed, was sentenced by the court, and executed — quartered), as well as the
2 CONC  maidservants Hannuska and Kaska. Szczęsny Charliński  was first wounded with a weapon and then strangled and killed by the servants.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the murder, the victim’s brothers — Krzysztof, Jan (podkomorzy of Lutsk), and Szymon (royal rotmistrz) Charlinski — who lived at the estate Skworcze, arrived at the scene. They discovered the body, restrained the servants, r
2 CONC eported the murder, and initiated a court investigation.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the investigation, accusations of involvement were also brought against Elena’s brother Paweł Monwid Dorohostayski. Several weeks before the murder, Elena had been staying at his estate Worotnevo, where their mother Ludmiła
2 CONC  Irikovna Dorohostayska also lived. According to the investigators, Paweł Monwid Dorohostayski may have encouraged the crime through his conversations.
