1 OCCU Mahmud Astrakhani (Urdu, Persian: محمود بن کوچک‎) was one of Küchük Muhammad's sons and a Khan who Founder of the Khanate of Astrakhan in the 1460s.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mahmud Astrakhani (Urdu, Persian: محمود بن کوچک‎) was one of Küchük Muhammad's sons and a Khan who founded the Khanate of Astrakhan in the 1460s. After years of struggle for the throne of the Great Horde against Ak
2 CONC hmat Khan, he escaped to the town of Hajji Tarkhan (or Xacitarxan), establishing the independent Khanate of Astrakhan there. Mahmud Astrakhani maintained friendly relations with his powerful neighbors—the Nogay Horde and the Great
2 CONC  Horde and coined his own money.
2 CONT
2 CONT His letter to the Ottoman Sultan Mehmed II (as dispatched on April 10, 1466) is a curious example of diplomatic epistles written in the 15th-century Old Tatar language. The content is a necessity of renewal of diplomatic relations
2 CONC  between Turkey and Astrakhan, and sending ambassadors to Istanbul.
2 CONT
2 CONT For uncertainties and additional information see the second part of List of Astrakhan khans.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Janibeg briefly ruled Crimea in the winter of 1476/77 until he was driven out by the legitimate ruler Nur Devlet.
2 CONT
