2 CONT externalfile:drive-3aee9e93dd168931eff71ff99c2a73e8c9317d8b/root/GENI/La lignée des Moghadam de Maragheh.mhtml
2 CONT  Il est marié a la soeur de Haj Ali Khan Etemad Saltaneh I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amir Bahador-Mir Panj
2 CONT
2 CONT =====
2 CONT دستۀ قزاق آذربایجان از عوض دستۀاردبیل و مشکین ابوابجمعی حسین پاشا خان امیر بهادر جنگ ref:  p. 50 https://iranianstudies.macmillan.yale.edu/sites/default/files/zamimeh-ye_ketab-e_tadvin.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT =====
2 CONT Petit fils de Ahmad Khan Biglerbeyg de l'Azarbaijan, par son pere. Arriere grand pere de Ali Mohammad Moghadam Maraghei-
2 CONT
2 CONT Son arrière grand père vint en Iran depuis le Caucase, après le traité de Torkmanshah et servit comme militaire, a la cour de Fath Ali Shah, du prince Abbas Mirza et de Mohammad Shah Qajar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Il est né en 1845 et a étudié, comme cela se faisait a cette époque, l'arabe, le persan et le Coran. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sous le prince Mozaffaredin (plus tard Shah), il entre au cabinet de Aghassi.  Ministre de l'Azerbaïdjan, general 2 étoiles, puis general adjudant de l'Azerbaïdjan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il obtient son titre de Amir Bahador sous Nasseredin Shah Qajar et accompagne ce dernier dans ses trois voyages en Europe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====
2 CONT Amir Bahadur (Hossein Pashakhan)
2 CONT  He was born in 1261 in Tabriz. His grandfather was a Caucasian reader who came to Iran with some people after the dirty Turkmenchay letter. During his reign, Mozaffar al-Din Shah in Tabriz held the position of Qollar Aghasi, the 
2 CONC Crown Prince, and after a while, at the suggestion of Amir Nezam Grossi, he became the Crown Prince. In the year 1310 AH. AH was named "Amir Bahador" by Naser al-Din Shah, and after the accession of Muzaffar al-Din Mirza, he becam
2 CONC e the head of the court guard house Amir Bahador in 1321 AH. AH replaced Mahmoud Hakim al-Molk, became minister and remained for three years /
2 CONT
2 CONT Amir Bahador, because of his deep religious beliefs and interest in the monarchy, was an opponent of the constitution and supported legitimacy. Obama became the Minister of War in the cabinet of Mushir al-Saltanah with the title o
2 CONC f "Grand Commander-in-Chief" after the cannonade of the parliament and the emergence of petty tyranny.
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined Mozaffar al-Din Shah, and on his travels abroad Shah Amir al-Bahadur received so many government and court badges and awards from the heads of other countries that in formal parties and ceremonies, in addition to both si
2 CONC des of his chest, he covered his formal and tapestry-embroidered dress with domestic and foreign insignia. / (His garden and mansion on Amirieh Street and in a place he was known by his own name. Amir Bahador returned to Iran afte
2 CONC r living in Europe for some time and in 1336 AH, he died in Tehran
