1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [... The eldest son of Mirza Ali Akbar Khan Motamed al-Wazarah, Asadullah Khan, nicknamed Mukarram al-Saltanah, was the father of Jamshid Alam, who was born in 1281 AH in Trabzon. He continued his education in Ista
2 CONC nbul and Beirut and became fluent in French, Arabic and Turkish. After returning to Iran (1307 AH), he first served as an intern at the Iranian embassy and then as a dinner manager at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. He worked for
2 CONC  a while in the translation department, but a little later he joined the army and was appointed as a special assistant to the Crown Prince Muzaffar al-Din Shah with the emblem and support of a brigadier general. At the beginning o
2 CONC f the constitution, he tried to be elected as a lawyer from Qazvin, but failed, 3 and continued to work in the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. 5 of his services caused him to be nicknamed Mukarram al-Saltanah in 1318 AH. 6 He was sur
2 CONC vived by two sons, Ali Akbar and Jamshid. Jamshid Alam was born in Van, Turkey in 1280 and continued his primary and secondary education in Iran at the Dar al-Fonun seminary. Then he went to France to continue his education and st
2 CONC udied medicine in Lyon, France and specialized in otolaryngology (1936). After returning to Iran, he was employed by the medical school of Tehran University….] 
