1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Kazimieras Leonas Sapiega (1607–1656) was a nobleman of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, a part of the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth, Royal Secretary and Grand Writer of Lithuania from 1631, Court Marshal of Lithuania from 1637, Dep
2 CONC uty Chancellor of Lithuania from 1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Lew Sapieha. Studied abroad. Sejm deputy in 1631. One of four executors of Władysław IV Waza's last will. Opponent of Janusz Radziwiłł; organized anti-Swedish resistance in Lithuania during The Deluge.
